@header {
    name: Erik Scholtz
    target_role: Systems and Infrastructure Engineer
    contact: erikscholtz23@gmail.com | linkedin.com/in/erikscholtz | github.com/erscholtz
}

@separator {
    title: -- SKILLS --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
}

@skills {
    languages: Languages: Rust, C, C++, Python
    systems: Systems: Linux kernel drivers, UEFI/EDK-II, QEMU, TPM2, IPC, JSON-RPC
    tools: Tools: Cargo, CMake, KBuild, Make, Meson, Git, Valgrind, SQLite
}

@separator {
    title: -- PROJECTS ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
}

@project {
    title: harnessd Autocomplete Daemon
    stack: Rust · Tokio · tree-sitter · SQLite · JSON-RPC
    link: [github](github.com/erscholtz/harnessd)

    - Engineered a Rust daemon with local IPC, lockfile-based single-instance control, and graceful shutdown to serve editor and CLI requests over JSON-RPC 2.0.
    - Built a rusqlite proposal cache keyed by file path, byte range, and content hash, using indexed lookups and invalidation guards to keep completions fast, bounded, and coherent with source changes.
    - Used tree-sitter to resolve cursor byte offsets to AST regions and precompute cached suggestions from TODO/FIXME anchors across multiple languages.
}

@project {
    title: UEFI CVE Replication and Firmware Patch
    stack: C · EDK-II · QEMU · UEFI Secure Boot
    link: [github](github.com/erscholtz/uefi-cve-replication)

    - Replicated CVE-2022-21894 (Baton Drop) using QEMU; demonstrated vulnerability by safely sandboxing exploit payload in QEMU to understand attack vector.
    - Proposed proof-of-concept patch through monotonic counter in EDK-II using C on EFI file sign date timestamps preventing rollback attacks.
}

@project {
    title: Pyrus - Typesetting language and compiler
    stack: Rust · Recursive Descent Parsing · HIR · PDF Rendering
    link: [github](github.com/erscholtz/pyrus)

    - Zero-dependency compiler pipeline from lexer to parser to HIR for a typesetting language. Created this resume.
    - Implemented recursive descent parser with Pratt-style operator precedence and string interpolation support.
}

@project {
    title: Linux Character Device Driver
    stack: C · KBuild · Make · Linux Kernel APIs
    link: [github](github.com/erscholtz/linux-character-device-driver)

    - Implemented file operations using kernel APIs register_chrdev, class_create, and device_create.
    - Enabled dynamic runtime configuration through write operations allowing users to change output byte values.
    - Utilized kernel memory management functions copy_from_user and put_user for user-kernel space data transfer.
    - Built and deployed using kernel build system KBuild with Makefile automation.
}

